# Allowlist: send the build context only what the Dockerfile COPYs.
# Anything not listed below (git history, tests, CI config, caches, local env files,
# the stray zip and nested folder, images, lockfiles for tests...) never reaches the
# Docker daemon, so builds are faster and secrets in a local .env cannot leak into a layer.
#
# If you add a COPY to the Dockerfile, add its source here too.

*

# Packaging metadata and (optional) hash-pinned runtime lockfile
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!requirements.txt

# Application
!kamleon/
!alembic.ini
!migrations/
!gunicorn.conf.py
!entrypoint.sh

# Never ship bytecode or caches, even from inside the allowed folders
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
